// ctxc's parser is std's in a build program, so a library of the program's may have a
// namespace of the same name: it shadows ctxc's, in the checker and in C. An ordinary
// program has neither (case 02).
//
// The build program prints what its own `parser` and `syntax` give, 7 + 1, then the
// declarations it found, and generates their count for the executable to print. `ctxc run .`
// runs both; the `project` step runs the build program through `ctxc graph`, and `{t}` is the
// executable.
//# $ ctxc run .
//# stdout:
//| 8
//| file src/main.ctx
//| fn main @ src/main.ctx:1:1
//|   mut io: Io
//| 1
//# project
//# stdout:
//| 8
//| file src/main.ctx
//| fn main @ src/main.ctx:1:1
//|   mut io: Io
//# $ {t}
//# stdout:
//| 1
